<title>HONG KONG: Kee Shing interim net rises 15.5 percent.</title>
<headline>Kee Shing interim net rises 15.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   4.0    vs 4.1 (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.5    vs 1.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    17.75  vs 15.38 (see note)</p>
<p>    Turnover		     475.50 vs 536.81</p>
<p>    Company name		 Kee Shing (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  October 14-18</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 28</p>
<p>NOTE - Kee Shing trades in chemicals and metals for electroplating.</p>
<p>The group has adopted a new accounting policy by having its leasehold land amortised over their term of leases according to the Statement of Standard Accounting Practice No. 17.</p>
<p>In restating the imterim results of 1995, the charges of depreciation has been increased by HK$283,000 and the interim profit decreased by the same amount accordingly.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
